WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.513
Today is September 26, 2026.

3
00:00:07.513 --> 00:00:14.425
Overnight, Wall Street mounted a fragile relief rally, but underlying macro crosscurrents remain treacherous.

4
00:00:14.425 --> 00:00:20.025
The S and P five hundred and the tech heavy Nasdaq pushed higher, while the Dow lagged.

5
00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:26.336
Benchmark ten year Treasury yields marched upward, tightening financial conditions across the board.

6
00:00:26.336 --> 00:00:29.939
Headline sentiment found brief relief from Tehran.

7
00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:35.822
Iranian officials floated a seven day diplomatic framework to reopen the Strait of Hormuz.

8
00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:41.312
Crude oil ticked down in response, giving equity bulls a temporary window to breathe.

9
00:00:41.312 --> 00:00:45.883
Yet institutional desks view this detente as structurally fragile.

10
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:50.675
Gulf allies are urging Washington to maintain full economic pressure.

11
00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:55.993
The White House is leveraging dollar clearing sanctions against Iranian state aircraft.

12
00:00:55.993 --> 00:01:03.383
JPMorgan warned oil modeling is breaking down, keeping extreme one hundred fifty dollar barrel scenarios on the table.

13
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:08.334
Domestically, macroeconomic realities delivered a sharp reality check.

14
00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:14.902
The University of Michigan consumer sentiment index tumbled to forty-eight point one, a four month trough.

15
00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:19.523
Year ahead inflation expectations jumped to four point six percent.

16
00:01:19.523 --> 00:01:26.214
Five to ten year inflation expectations climbed to three point four percent, the highest print since May.

17
00:01:26.214 --> 00:01:31.226
Surging diesel and gasoline prices are squeezing household balance sheets.

18
00:01:31.226 --> 00:01:34.179
Mortgage rates breached seven percent.

19
00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:42.758
A brief uptick in durable goods purchases reflects panic buying ahead of anticipated price hikes, rather than genuine consumer strength.

20
00:01:42.758 --> 00:01:52.182
This sticky inflation print complicates the Federal Reserve rate path, pushing rate cut expectations further out and weighing on long duration valuations.

21
00:01:52.182 --> 00:01:57.648
This macro liquidity squeeze is directly reshaping tech sector capital allocation.

22
00:01:57.648 --> 00:02:02.317
Speculative software narratives are giving way to raw compute certainty.

23
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:08.052
Meta revealed acute capacity bottlenecks within its Mius artificial intelligence platform.

24
00:02:08.052 --> 00:02:14.020
Serving fewer than one million users, the platform suffered widespread service degradation.

25
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.069
Meta assigns dedicated virtual machines to each user for data privacy.

26
00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:25.111
This architecture causes compute consumption to scale linearly without shared workload efficiency.

27
00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:28.101
The immediate market takeaway is clear.

28
00:02:28.101 --> 00:02:33.665
Artificial intelligence applications cannot scale without massive physical infrastructure.

29
00:02:33.665 --> 00:02:40.368
Capital is aggressively rotating out of unproven software layers and returning to pick and shovel hardware plays.

30
00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:44.866
Simultaneously, regulatory crosscurrents are intensifying.

31
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:51.177
Tech heavyweights Google, OpenAI, and Anthropic formed the Frontier AI Standards Board.

32
00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:57.415
This self regulatory body aims to establish safety benchmarks and incident reporting protocols.

33
00:02:57.415 --> 00:03:05.687
Big tech is moving proactively to shape upcoming compliance frameworks, raising barriers to entry for smaller open source competitors.

34
00:03:05.687 --> 00:03:10.797
In long term infrastructure, Google tested its space data center prototype.

35
00:03:10.797 --> 00:03:18.971
A satellite carrying four TPU chips launched aboard a SpaceX rocket to test orbital cooling and cosmic radiation resilience.

36
00:03:18.971 --> 00:03:23.248
Current thermal constraints limit active compute to fifteen minutes.

37
00:03:23.248 --> 00:03:27.721
Cisco stands positioned for future ground to orbit network routing.

38
00:03:27.721 --> 00:03:33.113
However, orbital compute remains a distant call option rather than near term revenue.

39
00:03:33.113 --> 00:03:37.219
Turning to our pivotal equity deep dives for the trading session.

40
00:03:37.219 --> 00:03:39.474
First, Nvidia.

41
00:03:39.474 --> 00:03:47.292
Ticker N-V-D-A. Meta compute bottlenecks reaffirm that hyperscalers must keep spending aggressively on advanced accelerators.

42
00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:52.709
Nvidia remains the primary institutional beneficiary of this structural shortage.

43
00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:59.829
Institutional flows continue to treat Nvidia as the ultimate cash flow anchor in artificial intelligence hardware.

44
00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:06.324
Technical support sits firmly at one hundred fifteen dollars, backed by its fifty day moving average.

45
00:04:06.324 --> 00:04:10.552
Heavy overhead resistance looms at one hundred thirty dollars.

46
00:04:10.552 --> 00:04:15.013
A breakout above one hundred thirty opens the path to fresh highs.

47
00:04:15.128 --> 00:04:18.668
Risk management boundaries must remain disciplined.

48
00:04:18.618 --> 00:04:28.202
Should sticky inflation push ten year Treasury yields above four point six percent, multiple compression could test secondary support down at one hundred eight dollars.

49
00:04:28.202 --> 00:04:31.032
Second, Meta Platforms.

50
00:04:31.032 --> 00:04:32.773
Ticker M-E-T-A.

51
00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:35.983
The market faces a fundamental divergence.

52
00:04:35.983 --> 00:04:42.184
The Mius bottleneck exposes rising capital expenditure intensity without immediate monetization.

53
00:04:42.184 --> 00:04:49.415
Positively, expanding immersive hardware ecosystems drives long term content and engine licensing demand.

54
00:04:49.415 --> 00:04:53.005
Yet near term margin expansion faces friction.

55
00:04:53.005 --> 00:04:58.496
Technically, Meta is testing key horizontal support at four hundred ninety dollars.

56
00:04:58.496 --> 00:05:02.111
Resistance is capped at five hundred twenty dollars.

57
00:05:02.111 --> 00:05:06.204
Traders should watch the four hundred ninety dollar floor closely.

58
00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:11.192
A break below risks a rapid gap fill toward four hundred seventy dollars.

59
00:05:11.192 --> 00:05:13.373
Third, Alphabet.

60
00:05:13.373 --> 00:05:22.172
Ticker G-O-O-G-L-E. Google is playing offense across multiple horizons, from orbital TPU prototypes to frontline regulatory leadership.

61
00:05:22.172 --> 00:05:30.052
While orbital data centers generate zero near term earnings, Google core cash flows comfortably fund ambitious exploration.

62
00:05:30.052 --> 00:05:38.189
Technically, Alphabet trades in a defined channel between one hundred sixty dollars support and one hundred seventy-five dollars resistance.

63
00:05:38.189 --> 00:05:41.523
Institutional accumulation remains steady.

64
00:05:41.523 --> 00:05:47.969
A close below one hundred fifty-eight dollars signals macro multiple contraction across mega cap tech.

65
00:05:47.969 --> 00:05:52.037
In this environment, macro liquidity dictates terms.

66
00:05:52.037 --> 00:05:57.515
Stick with real earnings, proven hardware moats, and pristine balance sheets.

67
00:05:57.515 --> 00:06:01.523
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

68
00:06:01.523 --> 00:06:05.689
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
